- op: discuss  # 3722
  at: '2026-09-02T05:39:35Z'  # 3722
  by: agent  # 3722
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3722
  clock: 7  # 3722
  nonce: '3722'  # 3722
  message: "SATISFIED in PR merged as dev 28998e145c. Behavioural evidence below, on the\nMERGED tree, every case cold in its own XDG_CACHE_HOME (each asserts its own\n\"No cached results found\"), with a live control in the same discipline.\n\nTHE ITEM'S OWN REPRO, RE-RUN, all four names its statement lists:\n\n    s <- getLine     ; writeFile  -> 2 io edges: fs_write + ipc_recv Prelude.getLine\n    c <- getChar     ; writeFile  -> 2 io edges: fs_write + ipc_recv Prelude.getChar\n    s <- getContents ; writeFile  -> 2 io edges: fs_write + ipc_recv Prelude.getContents\n    n <- readLn      ; writeFile  -> 2 io edges: fs_write + ipc_recv Prelude.readLn\n  CONTROL\n    s <- readProcess \"uname\" [] \"\" -> 2 io edges: fs_write + subprocess\n  NEGATIVE CONTROL (the deliberate exclusion, below)\n    c <- lines <$> getContents     -> 1 io edge: fs_write only\n\nBefore this change every one of the first four produced ONE edge (the sink\nonly). The discriminator was application-with-arguments, exactly as filed.\n\nTHE QUALIFIED QUESTION THIS ITEM LEFT UNMEASURED IS ANSWERED: YES.\n\"ALSO OBSERVED, NOT COUNTED: several sites are QUALIFIED (T.getLine,\nBS.getContents) ... Whether they share the mechanism is UNMEASURED.\" They do,\nand they are now reachable on their own rows:\n\n    import qualified Data.Text.IO as T ; s <- T.getLine\n      -> ipc_recv Data.Text.IO.getLine   (not Prelude's row -- the alias is\n         kept separate from the name rather than folded into it, because\n         folding produces \"T.getLine\" in the NAME slot, which is INV-januj's\n         defect in a new place)\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. The analyzer now emits a calls edge for a bare identifier in the\nthree positions where it is unambiguously EXECUTED -- the right-hand side of a\n`<-` bind, a bare `do` statement, and the argument of a combinator whose only\npurpose is to run an action (void/forever/liftIO/try/replicateM{,_}) -- and\nFAILS CLOSED on a name the enclosing definition binds for itself (a `<-`\nbinder, a parameter, a let/where binding), which is the rule\n_hs_classify_handle_text already states in this module for the same reason:\nthe seam ADDS edges.\n\nA/B, eight repositories, both arms cold, baseline asserted by GREPPING THE\nRUNTIME FILE rather than trusting the branch name:\n\n    1,916 -> 2,239 io chains, +323, ZERO LOST.\n\nAll 323 are haskell. Three read back against source rather than asserted:\n  simplex-chat src/Simplex/Chat/Bot.hs:35  race_ (forever $ void getLine)\n  stack        src/Stack/FileWatch.hs:108  l <- getLine\n  yesod        yesod-bin/AddHandler.hs:73  name <- getLine inside a let-bound do\n\n*** TWO CORRECTIONS TO THIS ITEM'S OWN RECORD. ***\n\n(1) THE FILED POPULATION IS DOUBLE-COUNTED. This item's tally reads\n\"cohort6_crypto 6, simplex-chat 6\" -- but\nALL_REPOS/plazaflow_deep_repos/simplex-chat is a SYMLINK into\ncohort6_crypto/simplex-chat/, and all 267 of cohort6_crypto's .hs files live\nunder it. The two paths are one repository, so those are the same six sites\ncounted twice: 25 sites over 9 repositories is 19 over 8. The corpus-is-\nsymlinked landmine in the form that inflates a count rather than hanging a\nwalk. I made the identical mistake first -- a pass of my own measurement\nreported 794 catalogued sites where there are 505 -- and caught it only\nbecause `find` reported simplex-chat as zero files.\n\nThe previous entry's \"THE FILED FIGURE REPRODUCES -- this is a confirmation,\nnot a correction\" was therefore itself built on the inflated count. Its\nsubstantive point stands and is untouched: a `<-`-only scan IS the wrong\ninstrument, and finds 9 of the real sites.\n\n(2) THE POPULATION IS 505 SITES, NOT 19, BECAUSE THE MECHANISM IS NOT ABOUT\nTHESE FOUR NAMES. Every zero-argument row in haskell.yaml was hidden by it.\nMeasured over the eight distinct repositories, catalogued sites in the three\ncovered positions:\n\n    getCurrentTime 220 | getCurrentDirectory 20 | getArgs 17\n    getEnvironment 17  | exitFailure 16         | exitSuccess 10\n    getProgName 9      | getLine 6 (chains)     | getExecutablePath 3\n    getTemporaryDirectory 3 | getHomeDirectory 1 | newManager 1\n\ngetArgs is a canonical untrusted-input source in its own right and was as dead\nas getLine. This item's \"the reason to file is not volume\" holds -- but the\nvolume was there anyway and nobody had counted it.\n\nRESIDUAL, FILED SEPARATELY, NOT SILENTLY ACCEPTED. The infix operators are\nEXCLUDED on measurement: `<$>` 35.3% of sites name a locally-bound value,\n`>>=` 32.9%, `<*>` 32.6%, against 11.3/15.2/15.5% for the three covered\npositions. Haskell spells fmap over Maybe, lists and Either with the same\noperators it spells IO with, so without types the two are indistinguishable;\ntogether they would add 63 catalogued sites for 3,812 more at 18-35% wrong,\nagainst the 442 of 505 the covered positions already reach. That is a\nSITE-level recall gap, not a primitive-level reachability gap, so it does not\nhold this item's statement open -- each of the four names is reachable by some\ncall site. Pinned by test_infix_operand_is_deliberately_excluded so a later\nreader must re-measure rather than assume.\n\nALSO FOUND WHILE HERE, filed rather than chased:\n  * the haskell analyzer emits one calls edge PER CURRIED APPLY LEVEL, so\n    `readProcess \"uname\" [] \"\"` produces three identical edges (same id) and\n    `writeFile \"o\" s` two;\n  * System.Exit's exitWith/exitFailure/exitSuccess/die are rowed env_write,\n    which a process exit is not -- 26 of the newly-reachable chains."  # 3722
